WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.346
Teacher midterm practice, question 11.

2
00:00:03.966 --> 00:00:06.923
In Figure 1, at point C, what has the metal done,

3
00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:09.299
and what happens when the load is removed?

4
00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:13.112
C lies beyond the yield point B.

5
00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:16.743
So the metal has stretched both elastically and plastically.

6
00:00:17.364 --> 00:00:22.761
Unloading from C follows the dashed line parallel to the elastic slope, down to H.

7
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.371
So H is the permanent strain.

8
00:00:25.371 --> 00:00:29.961
I, directly below C, is the total strain while the load is still on.

9
00:00:31.561 --> 00:00:35.724
The answer is E: elastic and plastic, with a permanent strain H.

10
00:00:36.544 --> 00:00:40.310
Do not read the permanent strain from the vertical drop at I.

11
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:44.243
Unloading always follows the line parallel to the elastic slope.
